         `End`-action restricted along `gen ↪ End`). The Clifford relation holds
         INSIDE `gen` (`clifford_in_gen`); the module action of a generator recovers
         the octonion left-multiplication (`gen_smul_Lop` : `g • y = a · y`); and
         `gen` is genuinely NON-commutative (`gen_noncomm`), so the module is not a
         trivial scalar action — it carries the same octonionic non-associativity
         that stopped the cascade.

  THE MOAT — posit-vs-derive (docs/STANDARD.md §0). The division-algebra-physics
